<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>EU leaders tussle over whom to send to Ukraine, Russia peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b3aa54d71b269905f23be78727de36deeea978cdd2b1a70bddfd301aba8554e</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468--127d08162dcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A seat at the table for Europe now appears likely following comments by a US envoy who just held talks with Putin. But who will take that seat remains unclear.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Czechia braces for massive protest as anger over government's public media reform plans boils</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef9d5f421882277ca38e29f02d16bbba066f74c3143324ca0fd2ae4a1c1431a8</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T18:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-as-anger-over-government-s-public-media-reform-plans-boils/a-79933533--18522f8b244d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-as-anger-over-government-s-public-media-reform-plans-boils/a-79933533?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fast-tracked bill on public media funding reform has sparked strikes, rallies and fears for the independence of public broadcasting in Czechia. A massive protest is due to take place in Prague on November 15.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can the EU make it harder to trick consumers online?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22fd9efa59312270c839d28d4982943f48aea3eef9f45732b3e9241929f8dcaa</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T17:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-eu-make-it-harder-to-trick-consumers-online/a-79933447--856c99598d6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-the-eu-make-it-harder-to-trick-consumers-online/a-79933447?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants to curb subscription traps, misleading sales tactics and features that keep people scrolling. What would the proposed Digital Fairness Act change, and does it go far enough?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What have the talks with Russia and the US in Abu Dhabi achieved for Ukraine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64b0e7ddb75e8ddbc97982a31c429e4d7bdce7f1de8f73b082803eb4d4bbed02</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-have-the-talks-with-russia-and-the-us-in-abu-dhabi-achieved-for-ukraine/a-79930613--89b8a9b8f641.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-have-the-talks-with-russia-and-the-us-in-abu-dhabi-achieved-for-ukraine/a-79930613?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The first trilateral talks between Ukraine, the US and Russia in nine months have ended with an agreement on exchanging prisoners. Does this mark a genuine breakthrough and a step toward peace?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary eases abortion restrictions in women's rights overhaul</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cf46bc9d8e342fd5f32b21658aad8ff2fa62f0be2c092903c1b973da6ec10a9</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:59:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-eases-abortion-rules/a-79931614--3bb42fe8feff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-eases-abortion-restrictions-in-women-s-rights-overhaul/a-79931614?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The reforms mark a break the the conservative policies of former PM Viktor Orban. The controversial "heartbeat regulation" is to be scrapped and women are to be better protected against violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: Rights groups sound alarm over proposed anti-terror law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30a8bc7236a5534c606594caa1e29e8c71b24c2065536eb18850414d0ce23f02</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227--abd4d2b11674.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Sri Lankan government is looking to replace a controversial anti-terror law, but critics say the new one is just as bad.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK court convicts 2 Iranian men of spying on journalists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3396046f7799983df8595bcc1b3421ce8e464a8948e829898a2f08aa19e496a2</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583--9da85f420d5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has found two Iranian citizens guilty of surveilling reporters for a Persian-language television station critical of Iran's government. One was also convicted of planning a violent attack against them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: Spy row, second affair leaves Nvidia without its rockstar CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5a8f67e72d43fd27ca3ddb391c0b82394e3eadcadd0610fd509d1ccacbf4e6f</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-second-affair-leaves-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972--471686cc8872.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-second-affair-leaves-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang, who built Nvidia into the world’s dominant AI chipmaker, is stepping down as CEO after a second affair came to light. DW examines how losing its figurehead will affect the firm and the US-China AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Exiled journalists still repressed by regime</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cff57f812547b827d5730ce2dd9a3a915d3f75251071b5602278f6f8b548cc8b</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694--82c71d3aa718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For many independent reporters, leaving Iran does not mean fully escaping the grasp of the Iranian state. The regime uses family members, bank accounts and the property they left behind to apply pressure across borders.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China's Xi Jinping renews calls for 'reunification' with Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f5030ac0c9fc0f177e3598b931c4417f81028bf7ac4c238ad123449812111e2</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-jinping-renews-calls-for-reunification-with-taiwan/a-79929738--c3c1f561b896.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-jinping-renews-calls-for-reunification-with-taiwan/a-79929738?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Xi Jinping said that reunification was inevitable, but stopped short of mentioning military force. Taiwan though swiftly rejected Beijing's demands as tensions continue over the island's future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Israel strikes Gaza hospital, says Hamas senior figure inside</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67673a2b65fa5dab21663b32132dbeaaa50ccfb58fbe68b9743bce685a712604</id><updated>2026-11-13T06:58:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-strikes-gaza-hospital-says-hamas-senior-figure-inside/a-79927645--35a0867b6650.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-strikes-gaza-hospital-says-hamas-senior-figure-inside/a-79927645?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israel says Hamas was using the hospital as a military command center, while Palestinian officials report at least six people killed, including a surgeon. The strike comes amid an increasingly fragile ceasefire.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
